From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Matthew Feickert <matthew.feickert@cern.ch>
Date: Thu, 1 Oct 2026 17:52:39 -0600
Subject: [PATCH] Link the Fortran runtime by name

FLDFLAGS is scraped from the verbose output of the Fortran compiler's link
step, so it holds absolute paths into the build environment, including
the compiler version, and libraries that are internal to the compiler.
These get written into the installed fcc script, where they do not exist
at install time. As LDFLAGS already has the library search path, keep
only the names of the Fortran runtime libraries that the compiler links.
libquadmath is among them on the platforms where REAL*16 needs it.

On macOS the C compiler that fcc calls is clang, which does not link the
GCC runtime that the Fortran compiler links from its own directory. The
REAL*16 arithmetic (__addtf3, ...) is in it, so link the shared GCC
runtime there.
---
 configure | 16 ++++------------
 1 file changed, 4 insertions(+), 12 deletions(-)

diff --git a/configure b/configure
index 7bb6321..1200bee 100755
--- a/configure
+++ b/configure
@@ -208,23 +208,15 @@ while read line ; do
   [[ "$1" =~ (/collect2|/ld|^ld)$CONF_EXE$ ]] && while test $# -gt 1 ; do
     shift
     case "$1" in
-    *.o | -lc*)
-      ;;
-    -l* | -L* | *.a)
+    -lgfortran | -lquadmath | -lm)
       FLDFLAGS+=" $1" ;;
-    -Bstatic | -Bdynamic | *.ld)
-      FLDFLAGS+=" -Wl,$1" ;;
-    /*)
-      FLDFLAGS+=" -L$1" ;;
-    -rpath*)
-      FLDFLAGS+=" -Wl,$1,$2"
-      shift ;;
-    -dynamic-linker)
-      shift ;;
     esac
   done
 done < <(eval $CONF_FC$CONF_FFLAGS -v -o $test $test.f 2>&1)
 
+# clang does not link the GCC runtime, which has the REAL*16 arithmetic
+test "$CONF_OS" = Darwin && FLDFLAGS+=" -lgcc_s.1.1"
+
 eval setflags LDFLAGS "$LDFLAGS $CONF_LDFLAGS $FLDFLAGS"
 
 echo "ok" 1>&3
